-- title:
--   Degree of the q↦ q^ℓ degeneracy map over L
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $A$ be a natural number that is nonzero, and let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $F^{\mathrm{full}}_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set `divisorExpansions N`, and for an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ write $L\cdot F_0$ for `laurentBaseChange L F₀`, the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb L` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ into $L((q))$. The map `heckeBetaBar L A ℓ` is the $L$-algebra homomorphism $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{A}\to L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{A\ell}$ induced by `qExpand L ℓ`, the ring endomorphism of $L((q))$ that rescales exponents by $\ell$, i.e. $f(q)\mapsto f(q^{\ell})$. The assertion is that `finrankAlong` of this map, namely the $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{A}$-module rank of $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{A\ell}$ for the algebra structure transported along `heckeBetaBar L A ℓ`, equals $\ell$ if $\ell \mid A$ and $\ell+1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the degree of the degeneracy map $X_0(A\ell)\to X_0(A)$, $\tau\mapsto\ell\tau$, namely $\psi(A\ell)/\psi(A)$, formulated over an arbitrary field $L$ of characteristic zero rather than over $\mathbb{Q}$ alone; it is one of the two degree inputs for the Hecke correspondence $T_\ell$ on these Laurent-series models. It is used by the place-specialization and fibre-model lemmas that analyse how places of the modular function field prolong along $\beta_\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrankAlong_heckeBetaBar.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_DegeneracyTower
